// Shared app configuration.
//
// The Discogs token ships with the app again, because routing every search
// through the backend cost more than it was worth — see DiscogsClient.get.
// It is scrambled rather than written out in the clear, so it is not readable
// with `strings` or `plutil`; that is a speed bump, not secrecy, and the token
// should be treated as one that will eventually leak. Regenerate the blob with
//
//     ./Scripts/obfuscate-token.py <token>
//
// and keep the result in Secrets.xcconfig, which is gitignored. Never put it
// here: an obfuscated credential in a tracked file is a published credential
// with extra steps. An empty default keeps a clean checkout building.
DISCOGS_TOKEN_OBFUSCATED =
#include? "Secrets.xcconfig"

// Supabase identifies Indigo's own backend, and both values below ship in
// every build by design: the ref appears in the URL of each request, and the
// publishable key is the client key Supabase expects to be public. Row Level
// Security is what actually guards the data, so these live here rather than
// in Secrets.xcconfig — hiding them would break clean checkouts and buy no
// safety. The service-role key is the real secret and must never come near
// this file.
//
// MUST be the bare project ref, never the full URL. A `//` opens a comment in
// xcconfig, so pasting https://<ref>.supabase.co here truncates the value to
// `https:` and the build still succeeds. SupabaseConfiguration assembles the
// URL from this ref and rejects anything that is not ref-shaped.
SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF = leynozulpkjuufbbjjpa
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY = sb_publishable_hP8GTN5m8YygAs6GzTbm0Q_sqkZPjzi
